What are the major growth drivers?
Major drivers include electric vehicle adoption, demand for high-efficiency power conversion, renewable-energy deployment, EV charging infrastructure, data-center power requirements, grid modernization, and improving SiC manufacturing yields.
What are the emerging applications?
Emerging applications include AI and data-center power infrastructure, 5G base-station power systems, offshore-wind converters, rail electrification, and advanced grid infrastructure.
What are the key challenges?
Major challenges include manufacturing complexity, yield variability, high semiconductor-fab capital requirements, limited high-purity SiC substrate supply, and competition from alternative wide-bandgap technologies such as gallium nitride in selected lower-voltage applications.
